# Apple Pear Crisp

Based on [Rustic Apple & Pear Crisp - The Simple Veganista](https://simple-veganista.com/rustic-apple-pear-crisp) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251118014236/https://simple-veganista.com/rustic-apple-pear-crisp/))

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Filling

- [ ] 3 medium [apples]{ ing="apples" }, cored and chopped
- [ ] 3 medium [pears]{ ing="pears" }, cored and chopped
- [ ] 3 Tbsp fresh [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [sugar]{ ing="sugar" } (coconut or organic cane)
- [ ] 1 heaping tsp [cinnamon]{ ing="cinnamon" }

### Topping

- [ ] 1 3/4 cups [old fashioned oats]{ ing="old-fashioned-oats" }
- [ ] 1/4 cup [almond meal]{ ing="almond-meal" } or flaxseed meal (optional)
- [ ] 1 cup [finely chopped walnuts]{ ing="finely-chopped-walnuts" } (optional)
- [ ] 1/2 cup [pure maple syrup]{ ing="pure-maple-syrup" }
- [ ] 3-4 Tbsp [coconut oil]{ ing="coconut-oil" } (room temperature)
- [ ] 1 tsp [vanilla extract]{ ing="vanilla-extract" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [mineral salt]{ ing="mineral-salt" }
- [ ] [Cinnamon]{ ing="garnish-cinnamon" } for garnish

## Recipe

1. Preheat oven to 350F.
1. Wash, core, and dice the [apples]{ ing="apples" } and [pears]{ ing="pears" }.
1. Combine fruit with [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }, [sugar]{ ing="sugar" }, and [cinnamon]{ ing="cinnamon" } in a 9x9 baking dish.
1. In a separate bowl, mix [oats]{ ing="old-fashioned-oats" }, [almond meal]{ ing="almond-meal" }, [walnuts]{ ing="finely-chopped-walnuts" }, [maple syrup]{ ing="pure-maple-syrup" }, [coconut oil]{ ing="coconut-oil" }, vanilla, and [salt]{ ing="mineral-salt" }. Spread over fruit.
1. Sprinkle with additional [cinnamon]{ ing="garnish-cinnamon" } for garnish.
1. Bake 35-40 minutes until fruit is fork-tender.
1. Cool 5-10 minutes before serving.

## Notes

1. Serves 6 generously in about 50 minutes total
1. Suggested serving size: 1/6 of the crisp (about 3/4 cup)
1. Per serving: 344 calories, 4.4g protein, 22.1g fat, 36g carbs, 4.9g fiber
1. Uses natural sweeteners (maple syrup) and minimal added sugar compared to traditional crisps
1. Vegan and can be made gluten-free by using certified gluten-free oats
